{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1025619-bloodline-conversion-the-cockscomb-society","id":1025619,"title":"Bloodline Conversion- The Cockscomb Society","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-02T16:28:01-08:00","id":1025619,"title":"Bloodline Conversion- The Cockscomb Society","content":"Hey, everybody! Hope you all had a good New Year! Today, I'm giving you my conversion of the Cockscomb Society, a Nosferatu bloodline who play against type and strive to be socially active, to the point that they get Majesty as a bloodline discipline! <br /> <br /> This conversion was relatively easy. I tweaked the Bloodline Bane to reflect the fact that Virtues and Vices are no longer systems in Requiem 2e. Now, instead of being unable to get Willpower from their Virtue, Cockscomb Gals and Gents have a much harder time getting Willpower from their Mask, which I think stays true to their fluff of not quite &quot;getting&quot; human behavior, and what it means to be human. <br /> <br /> The Devotion they got was a nice way of blending Majesty and Nightmare, but we already have Devotions that combine those. So I made it a more general-purpose ability that can allow them to alleviate or even overcome the penalties to their Social rolls. <br /> <br /> As always, leave thoughts, comments, and likes. Next week, you'll be getting the Lygos, Nosferatu who take the clan's &quot;monsters in the shadows&quot; stereotype to its logical conclusion! <br /> <br /> <br /> <u><b>Bloodline Conversion- The Cockscomb Society</b></u><br /> <i>Life is hell. Good thing we're dead, right? </i><br /> <br /> The Nosferatu of the bloodline known as the Cockscomb Society are realists among their clan. To them, their curse is not so insurmountable that it consigns them to a future as vermin living in sewers, but neither is it a secret blessing that makes them leper kings. They reject the necropoli of the larger clan, choosing to live among humans, the better to remind themselves of their former humanity, and to make it harder for them to slip down to the bottom rung of the All-Night Society. Unfortunately, the Cockscomb Gals and Gents seem to have forgotten what being human really means. To them, it is not about clinging to one's humanity and resisting the Beast, but about having a nice house, an expensive car, going for nights out on the town, and keeping up with human trends and fashions.<br /> <br /> <b>Background: </b>The Cockscomb Society was originated by Potter Woolsthorpe Wycombe, an upper-class Nosferatu living in late-Victorian England. Wycombe was a contact of the Ashwoode Abbey, and provided the hunters with vampires, typically political rivals and personal enemies, for their \u201centertainment.\u201d Wycombe was paid handsomely for betraying his own kind over to humans who, at times, seemed capable of deeds more depraved than any vampire. Then, one night, Wycombe had a revelation. Sanctified say that he was visited by an angel of the Lord, who chastised him for his evil deeds and commanded him to mend his ways. Others say that he encountered a Strix, who seemed almost pleased with his behavior. Whatever the case, he rejected his despicable activities, and dedicated himself and his childer to upstanding behavior- not moral behavior, but socially acceptable conduct.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, Wycombe and his childer are not as successful as he would like. Whatever the reason, perhaps a permanent alteration of his Vitae due to exposure to the secret depravity of the Abbey, Cockscombs do not reap much benefit from acting according to their mortal Masks; to them, it is nothing more than that, a formality of engaging with humanity like wearing a suit or dress to a formal function. It is far easier for them to slip into the hidden truth of their Dirge, often leading to a disconcerting dissonance between their public persona and their words and actions.<br /> <br /> <b>The Becoming: </b>The members of the Cockscomb Society are not necessarily Embraced into the bloodline. Many are members of the elite, whether they are industrial heirs, movie stars, or political rising stars, who are Embraced by a member of the larger clan out of spite or some other reason. Whatever the reason, many do not take well to the typical existence of the Nosferatu, and petition the Cockscomb Society for membership, desperate for some degree of normality in their Requiems. Some are occasionally Embraced directly into the bloodline, either as a favor or as an act of mercy or selfishness. Members of the Cockscomb Society often have high Social Attributes and Skills, with Merits like Fame, Resources, Allies, Retainer, Herd, and Haven.<br /> <br /> <b>In the Danse Macabre: </b>If any Nosferatu can be said to be truly <i>liked, </i>it's the Cockscomb Society. Yes, they're creepy as all get-out, but not necessarily any more than vampires are in general. They dress well, and they act just like any other Kindred- at least, they make an attempt to- and they don't revel in their otherness like some other Nosferatu do. Yes, they're uncanny, but all clans have their banes. The Cockscomb Society is quite active in Kindred politics, and they are often Masters of Elysium, or active in covenant politics- most join the Invictus, though some may become Carthians, and a rare few spiritual ones join the Lancea et Sanctum.<br /> <br /> <b>Clan: </b>Nosferatu<br /> <br /> <b>Nickname: </b>Gals and Gents (as in \u201cCockscomb Gal/Gent\u201d)<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline Bane: </b>The Cockscomb Gals and Gents may enjoy the finer things in life, but they have no true understanding of human nature; their public personas are little more than trappings of attitude and presentation, often jarringly at odds with their words and deeds. An action in accordance with a Cockscomb Gal's Mask that would normally restore one Willpower does not restore any Willpower, while an action in accordance with a Cockscomb Gal's Mask that would normally restore all Willpower restores only one Willpower.<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline Disciplines: </b><i>Majesty, </i>Nightmare, Obfuscate, Vigor<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline Gift: Cockscomb Charm</b><br /> Cockscomb Gals and Gents can employ their mental Disciplines to achieve a number of interesting effects, depending on the situation. By spending a Vitae, a Cockscomb Gal can make a Presence + Socialize + Discipline roll to achieve a goal for the remainder of the scene. Using Majesty allows the Cockscomb Gal to downplay her monstrous nature, granting her an aura of supernatural beauty, granting her a bonus to all Social rolls except Intimidate equal to successes rolled. Using Nightmare allows the Cockscomb Gal to paint herself as menacing and intimidating, granting her a bonus to all Intimidate rolls equal to successes rolled. Using Obfuscate can mask the worst aspects of her vampiric nature, allowing her to suppress her Predatory Aura and appear human to both humans and vampires alike.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T16:58:01-08:00","id":1025629,"title":"","content":"Adding Disciplines to certain Skill rolls or some other actions? A subtle, yet quite effective boon.<br /> <br /> Hmm... I should adopt that line of thinking to homebrewing the bloodline gifts of the &quot;Old&quot; Ventrue/Nosferatu/Gangrel&quot; bloodlines, imported from Masquerade.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T18:02:09-08:00","id":1025650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1025619-bloodline-conversion-the-cockscomb-society?p=1025629#post1025629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Adding Disciplines to certain Skill rolls or some other actions? A subtle, yet quite effective boon.<br /> <br /> Hmm... I should adopt that line of thinking to homebrewing the bloodline gifts of the &quot;Old&quot; Ventrue/Nosferatu/Gangrel&quot; bloodlines, imported from Masquerade.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you! Usually, when I convert a bloodline, I try to keep a bloodline discipline as a series of devotions. Bloodlines with a single new devotion usually ended up getting them folded into the 2e baseline disciplines, or 2e has devotions that basically replaces the bloodline's devotion, so I usually try to preserve the spirit of the devotion with a broader utility ability. I figured that applying Disciplines to Skill rolls was a good way to incapsulate the Cockscomb Society's flavor and the idea of them being socially-oriented Nosferatu, and that they would need some sort of ability that would allow them to overcome the Nosferatu's innate social handicap.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T04:33:42-08:00","id":1025845,"title":"","content":"Seems pretty legit. Just a quick question: how does your Bloodline Gift interacts with Awe and Dread Presence? Does it stack?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/822-daemonchrno","name":"DaemonChrno","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar822_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T06:01:31-08:00","id":1025876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DaemonChrno</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1025619-bloodline-conversion-the-cockscomb-society?p=1025845#post1025845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seems pretty legit. Just a quick question: how does your Bloodline Gift interacts with Awe and Dread Presence? Does it stack?</div> </div> </div> </div>OP authors have stated in the forums that benefits from multiple powers stack. So I would say yes, though you are free to home rule rules to balance that if you think it's too powerful. Say, if you have benefits that technically give you an Exceptional Success on one success, any failure could be a dramatic failure. That's how I'm doing it for my Galateid Mimic in my Promethean game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}